{"id":"refine_20260929134945324","summary":"Updated the global task-cfafe428 memory with the demonstrated interior-fill color rule and grid-validity check.","rationale":"The demos and successful test show that closed-outline interiors are filled, but the fill color is not always 7: 4×4 interiors use 2, while 5×5 and 1×1 interiors use 7. The successful output also followed a malformed-grid attempt, making exact row and column counts a useful validation safeguard.","expectedOutcome":"On future task-cfafe428 instances, fill only enclosed outline interiors, select 2 for even-area interiors and 7 for odd-area interiors as supported by these examples, preserve borders and background, and verify output dimensions before submission.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_cfafe428_square_outline_interiors_fill_7","title":"ARC task-cfafe428: fill closed outline interiors by area parity","content":"For task-cfafe428, identify closed square or rectangular outlines and fill only their enclosed interiors, preserving outline cells and all background/unrelated cells. Demonstrations show fill color depends on enclosed interior area parity: even-area interiors use color 2 (including 4×4 interiors), while odd-area interiors use color 7 (including 5×5 and 1×1 interiors). The fresh test was solved with the same rule: a 4×4 interior used 2, while the 5×5 and 1×1 interiors used 7. Before submitting, verify the output has exactly the input dimensions and every row has the correct width; a malformed row caused an invalid-grid submission.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Corrects the memory's overly broad fixed-color-7 rule using multiple demonstrations and a successfully solved recurrence, and preserves the evidenced output-shape validation lesson.","before":{"id":"arc_task_cfafe428_square_outline_interiors_fill_7","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-cfafe428: fill square-outline interiors with 7","content":"For task-cfafe428, grids use background color 8 and contain empty square outlines. Demonstrations show outlines of different sizes and border colors filled in their interior with color 7. Preserve the outline borders, background, and unrelated cells. On recurrence, identify the square outlines and fill their enclosed interior cells with 7; confirm bounds and preserve all other cells. This rule produced a correct test submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:38:43.170Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:38:43.170Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_task_cfafe428_square_outline_interiors_fill_7","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-cfafe428: fill closed outline interiors by area parity","content":"For task-cfafe428, identify closed square or rectangular outlines and fill only their enclosed interiors, preserving outline cells and all background/unrelated cells. Demonstrations show fill color depends on enclosed interior area parity: even-area interiors use color 2 (including 4×4 interiors), while odd-area interiors use color 7 (including 5×5 and 1×1 interiors). The fresh test was solved with the same rule: a 4×4 interior used 2, while the 5×5 and 1×1 interiors used 7. Before submitting, verify the output has exactly the input dimensions and every row has the correct width; a malformed row caused an invalid-grid submission.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:38:43.170Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:49:52.418Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682173/attempts/44ad28d291934fa5ac58a5f0a3f63632/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929135251151","summary":"Updated the global task-cfafe428 memory with the confirmed interior-area parity rule and this recurrence’s examples.","rationale":"The task was solved correctly on this recurrence: 2×2 interiors were filled with 2 and 3×3 interiors with 7, while borders and background were preserved. This confirms that fill color depends on the number of interior cells, not the outline color.","expectedOutcome":"On future task-cfafe428 instances, count the cells inside each enclosed square or rectangular outline, fill even-area interiors with 2 and odd-area interiors with 7, and preserve borders and unrelated cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"task_cfafe428_enclosed_regions_fill_by_interior_area_parity","title":"task-cfafe428: enclosed regions fill by interior area parity","content":"For task-cfafe428, detect closed square or rectangular outline frames and fill only their enclosed interior cells, preserving every border and all unrelated/background cells. Choose the fill color by the number of interior cells: even area → color 2; odd area → color 7. Recurrence confirmation: a 4×4 outline has a 2×2 (4-cell) interior filled with 2; a 5×5 outline has a 3×3 (9-cell) interior filled with 7. Apply the parity rule to the interior area, not the outline dimensions or outline color.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Records a correctly solved recurrence that confirms the existing parity rule with concrete even- and odd-area examples.","before":{"id":"task_cfafe428_enclosed_regions_fill_by_interior_area_parity","kind":"memory","title":"task-cfafe428: enclosed regions fill by interior area parity","content":"Continual-ARC task-cfafe428 validated rule. Detect rectangular/square outline frames and fill their enclosed interior cells, preserving every border and unrelated cell. Fill interior with 7 when interior area (number of cells) is odd; fill with 2 when interior area is even. Demonstration: 1-cell and 3x3 interiors ->7; 2x2 interior ->2. Applies to rectangles too (e.g., a 4x4 interior ->2). Isolated center/background-colored cells inside 3x3 color motifs are also interiors and should be changed. Important transcription lesson: preserve the actual frame coordinates; in the test a 3x3 frame at rows 7-9, cols 1-3 had center at row8 col2 and that cell became 7.","path":"arc/task-cfafe428","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:52:37.131072+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:52:37.131106+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"task_cfafe428_enclosed_regions_fill_by_interior_area_parity","kind":"memory","title":"task-cfafe428: enclosed regions fill by interior area parity","content":"For task-cfafe428, detect closed square or rectangular outline frames and fill only their enclosed interior cells, preserving every border and all unrelated/background cells. Choose the fill color by the number of interior cells: even area → color 2; odd area → color 7. Recurrence confirmation: a 4×4 outline has a 2×2 (4-cell) interior filled with 2; a 5×5 outline has a 3×3 (9-cell) interior filled with 7. Apply the parity rule to the interior area, not the outline dimensions or outline color.","path":"arc/task-cfafe428","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:52:37.131072+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:52:56.317Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682173/attempts/44ad28d291934fa5ac58a5f0a3f63632/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
