s one cell per panel. Demonstrations and the solved test support encoding panels with at least two sparse non-background marker cells as 1; a panel with exactly one marker retains the panel's background color (for example, the solved test output was [[1,1],[1,1],[1,4]]). Panel and background colors may vary across instances, so infer them from the input and demonstrations rather than hard-coding colors. Exclude separator lines when extracting panels, count marker cells within each panel, and verify output dimensions and classifications.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","evidence":"task-2810ce4d demonstrations and correctly solved test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:24.339Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:02:24.339Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682173/attempts/44ad28d291934fa5ac58a5f0a3f63632/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
