daries. Demo 2 extends the color-7 diagonal down-left, color-2 diagonal up-left, color-3 diagonal up-right, and color-4 diagonal down-left. Demo 3 extends color 7 down-left and color 6 up-right. In the successful 26×27 test, color 9 at (16,21),(17,22) extends up-left to the boundary; the adjacent vertical color-1 pair at (17,23),(18,23) and singleton color 5 at (18,22) remain unextended. Two guesses failed before the rule was established: preserving the input unchanged, and extending the vertical color-1 pair. Confidence: high for diagonal extension and not extending vertical/horizontal pairs or singletons; check each candidate line for obstacles and exact direction before applying.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","task_id":"task-90b841ed","confidence":"high"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T15:27:20.986Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T16:11:46.849Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682173/attempts/44ad28d291934fa5ac58a5f0a3f63632/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
